  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Strong name: Microsoft.Exchange.WebServices.NETStandard.dll and Sunsetless.Ews.Core.dll are signed with the Sunsetless key (public key token 1b8c25c6fc94dcf1), so strong-named .NET Framework applications and components can reference them. This changes the assembly identity: on .NET Framework, rebuild every project that references the library against this version, because assemblies compiled against 1.2.1 or earlier, or against the port (Microsoft.Exchange.WebServices.NETStandard 1.1.x), do not load the signed DLL. On .NET 8, 9 and 10 nothing changes, and libraries compiled against the port keep working without a rebuild. Components that ship the library can supply their own license key with SunsetlessEws.UseComponentLicense. FindItem cuts long extended property values (PR_BODY, PR_HTML and others) to 255 characters or 510 bytes in every query path, as Exchange Online does, and BodyType.HTML returns a plain-text message as HTML. GetConversationItems returns the extended properties of a message as Exchange Online does: only those in its conversation view, with strings cut to 255 characters, while meeting messages, posts and messages with voting come back in full. GetConversationItems orders nodes as Exchange Online does: newest first when no SortOrder is sent (the EWS Managed API overload that takes a list of conversations never sends one), replies newest first in TreeOrderAscending, and MaxItemsToReturn keeps the newest items. SUNSETLESS_BRIDGE_ALL_HOSTS=true (BridgeAllHosts in the options) sends calls to every host to Microsoft Graph, Exchange Server included, for applications that still call an Exchange Server URL after their mailboxes moved to Exchange Online. Supported operations, verification against live Exchange Online and known differences: https://sunsetless.com/compatibility",
